WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.479 --> 00:00:09.080
Let's go to the eight five zero area code.

00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:10.769
Caller from eight five zero.

00:00:10.769 --> 00:00:12.769
What's your name and where are you calling
from?

00:00:12.769 --> 00:00:18.210
David, this is Phillip and I'm calling from
Mississippi, I've got a Florida number there.

00:00:18.210 --> 00:00:19.759
They love my call.

00:00:19.759 --> 00:00:20.759
What's going on?

00:00:20.759 --> 00:00:21.880
Well, I've got two questions.

00:00:21.880 --> 00:00:26.910
First of all, did you see the news recently
where Trump actually admitted his game plan

00:00:26.910 --> 00:00:33.000
as far as this the Supreme Court take and
kind of taken going to the Supreme Court and

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:37.640
arguing against the Melling ballots and trying
to take over that way?

00:00:37.640 --> 00:00:38.640
Yep, absolutely.

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:39.640
So Trump.

00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:44.940
Trump has said he is counting on the court
system to help him in November.

00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:47.719
He says it's to prevent it from being rigged.

00:00:47.719 --> 00:00:49.989
Really, it's to rig it.

00:00:49.989 --> 00:00:52.920
And the federal appeals courts could be a
part of it.

00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:53.920
Who knows?

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:57.030
Depending on what happens, the Supreme Court
could be a part of it.

00:00:57.030 --> 00:00:58.030
Absolutely.

00:00:58.030 --> 00:00:59.030
Right.

00:00:59.030 --> 00:01:03.309
The second thing I want to address is that
it seems, though, the Republicans, the only

00:01:03.309 --> 00:01:05.220
way they can get ahead is through recruiting.

00:01:05.220 --> 00:01:09.320
At least that's the kind of like what conclusion
I'm coming to.

00:01:09.320 --> 00:01:13.730
I mean, over the last seven years, as I'm
sure you know, schools over the last seven

00:01:13.730 --> 00:01:18.900
elections, we've only had one Republican win
by popular vote.

00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:24.080
So this Electoral College and the gerrymander
mentoring and all the judges that recently

00:01:24.080 --> 00:01:28.550
McConnell is picking, it seems the whole game
plan is to stay in power with the Republicans,

00:01:28.550 --> 00:01:32.890
to stay in power just by trying to steal the
vote and oppressed the boats.

00:01:32.890 --> 00:01:38.110
And if you look at, you know, you look at
polls and CNN and Fox News and online, everybody

00:01:38.110 --> 00:01:39.110
plays left.

00:01:39.110 --> 00:01:40.110
Yeah.

00:01:40.110 --> 00:01:41.330
All the things that we won't.

00:01:41.330 --> 00:01:43.820
All the things everybody is actually voting
for.

00:01:43.820 --> 00:01:47.220
We're voting is easy is left leaning policies.

00:01:47.220 --> 00:01:51.740
But we don't see that reflected in the White
House because the voting is just it's not

00:01:51.740 --> 00:01:53.280
there, just not easy to vote.

00:01:53.280 --> 00:01:58.590
So I believe that if we can ever start having
a conversation about making voting a national

00:01:58.590 --> 00:02:02.870
holiday, about actually do we like Australia,
perhaps where they have a fine if you don't

00:02:02.870 --> 00:02:06.760
vote or have the day off and just make it
easier, more accessible?

00:02:06.760 --> 00:02:08.930
I think we could finally go in one direction.

00:02:08.930 --> 00:02:11.879
This country is sort of back and forth ridiculous.

00:02:11.879 --> 00:02:15.049
Stop every four to eight years and actually
get some David Pakman.

00:02:15.049 --> 00:02:18.680
Yeah, I think that's going to happen unless
we do something with the Supreme Court, which

00:02:18.680 --> 00:02:21.319
is kind of going to be very difficult now
at this point.

00:02:21.319 --> 00:02:25.140
Well, mandatory voting is kind of its own
question, and I think that that's a separate

00:02:25.140 --> 00:02:26.140
issue.

00:02:26.140 --> 00:02:31.800
But you've beautifully pointed out that we
have a system that we you know, we talk abstractly

00:02:31.800 --> 00:02:34.760
about checks and balances and all of this
stuff.

00:02:34.760 --> 00:02:45.879
But we have a system that in practice allows
a center left country to be run by right wing

00:02:45.879 --> 00:02:50.409
legislative bodies and judicial bodies because
of the things you're pointing out.

00:02:50.409 --> 00:02:57.140
If you look at gerrymandering, you have a
structural disadvantage for Democrats when

00:02:57.140 --> 00:03:01.760
it comes to what percentage of the vote do
they need to get in order to just have 50

00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:02.810
percent representation?

00:03:02.810 --> 00:03:10.439
You look at the Senate, the Senate, by giving
two senators to each state, dramatically overstates

00:03:10.439 --> 00:03:16.700
the power of these states with very few people
that still get two senators.

00:03:16.700 --> 00:03:19.731
And I think it was something like there were
enough you could have.

00:03:19.731 --> 00:03:26.730
The senators representing only 17 percent
of the population decide that Trump is getting

00:03:26.730 --> 00:03:32.330
acquitted in terms of impeachment because
of that imbalance and the fundamentally undemocratic

00:03:32.330 --> 00:03:34.239
nature of the Senate.

00:03:34.239 --> 00:03:39.510
You have the Electoral College, as you point
out, wherein you have a country that votes

00:03:39.510 --> 00:03:45.790
for Democrats many times and many of those
times a Republican is still elected president.

00:03:45.790 --> 00:03:50.329
So you've pointed out many of the ways in
which the country is not really democratically

00:03:50.329 --> 00:03:51.329
run.

00:03:51.329 --> 00:03:54.280
And it is a major problem.

00:03:54.280 --> 00:03:58.639
Right now, I just don't feel like we're going
to make any consistent progress forward, no

00:03:58.639 --> 00:04:01.290
matter what we do in the next four to eight
years, it can be undone.

00:04:01.290 --> 00:04:03.430
It's risk repeat, which keep going back and
forth.

00:04:03.430 --> 00:04:07.340
And it's very difficult to make this of progress
if we're not able to lead in one direction.

00:04:07.340 --> 00:04:12.590
Well, I do think that if Joe Biden wins and
Democrats take the Senate, you could definitely

00:04:12.590 --> 00:04:16.459
undo a bunch of the damage Trump has done
and make some progress.

00:04:16.459 --> 00:04:18.250
But let's not put the cart before the horse.

00:04:18.250 --> 00:04:21.070
Let's deal with November first and then see
where we are.

00:04:21.070 --> 00:04:22.070
Right.

00:04:22.070 --> 00:04:23.670
Thanks for taking my call, David.

00:04:23.670 --> 00:04:24.670
All right.

00:04:24.670 --> 00:04:25.670
Appreciate it.

00:04:25.670 --> 00:04:25.674
Thank you so much

